--- answer ---
The cause is clear: `removeOldest` at `simplelru/lru.go:169-173` removes the **front** of the list (`c.evictList.Front()`), but `Add` inserts new entries at the front (`PushFront`) and `MoveToFront` marks entries as most-recently used. Therefore the oldest (least recently used) entry should be at the **back** (`Back()`), not the front. Removing `Front()` evicts the most recently used entry.

`RemoveOldest`/`GetOldest`/`Keys`/`Values` already correctly treat the back as oldest, so `removeOldest` is the only outlier.Fixed. `simplelru.LRU.removeOldest` was removing `evictList.Front()` (the most recently used entry) instead of `evictList.Back()` (the least recently used). Changed `Front()` to `Back()`. Build, vet, and tests pass.